    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-06-07T13:21:59Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No, not at the moment I am afraid. It was the original behavior, but was changed in a0508610fbb0877e9b2a663c79e11ee106146a9a, as I tripped many times when switching sessions. I assume that intentional leaving the session should autowrite it (at least if `config.autowrite` is `true`).\r\n\r\nIn theory, I'd say that it might be better to have `read()` autowrite current session only if `config.autowrite = true`.\r\n\r\nIs it only a matter of personal preference to not autowrite current session when reading another or is there some particular use case or workflow that this is not aligned with?",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">No, not at the moment I am afraid. It was the original behavior, but was changed in <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/a0508610fbb0877e9b2a663c79e11ee106146a9a/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/a0508610fbb0877e9b2a663c79e11ee106146a9a\"><tt>a050861</tt></a>, as I tripped many times when switching sessions. I assume that intentional leaving the session should autowrite it (at least if <code class=\"notranslate\">config.autowrite</code> is <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In theory, I'd say that it might be better to have <code class=\"notranslate\">read()</code> autowrite current session only if <code class=\"notranslate\">config.autowrite = true</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is it only a matter of personal preference to not autowrite current session when reading another or is there some particular use case or workflow that this is not aligned with?</p>",
            "bodyText": "No, not at the moment I am afraid. It was the original behavior, but was changed in a050861, as I tripped many times when switching sessions. I assume that intentional leaving the session should autowrite it (at least if config.autowrite is true).\nIn theory, I'd say that it might be better to have read() autowrite current session only if config.autowrite = true.\nIs it only a matter of personal preference to not autowrite current session when reading another or is there some particular use case or workflow that this is not aligned with?",
