        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`: there is auto-write of current session in `read()` [only if `MiniSessions.config.autowrite` is `true`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/35e1767f4cd7dde51256eabae7349a5283a43cba/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L127-L128). This indeed makes a more coherent behavior, thanks for mentioning this use case!",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This should now be resolved on latest <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code>: there is auto-write of current session in <code class=\"notranslate\">read()</code> <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/35e1767f4cd7dde51256eabae7349a5283a43cba/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L127-L128\">only if <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniSessions.config.autowrite</code> is <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code></a>. This indeed makes a more coherent behavior, thanks for mentioning this use case!</p>",
            "bodyText": "This should now be resolved on latest main: there is auto-write of current session in read() only if MiniSessions.config.autowrite is true. This indeed makes a more coherent behavior, thanks for mentioning this use case!",
